# PengyOS — a user's desktop session, started by greetd (general.service).
# auth: the password typed into the login screen (COSMIC's greeter relays
# greetd's PAM prompt). Automatic login (greetd's initial_session, opt-in:
# pengyos-autologin) opens the session without authenticating.
# pam_unix verifies an unprivileged user's password through the setuid
# unix_chkpwd (Server layer permissions.txt). pam_systemd turns the session
# into a logind session on seat0: /run/user/UID, the user's systemd manager,
# polkit's "active session", screen locking.
auth      requisite pam_nologin.so
auth      required  pam_unix.so
account   required  pam_unix.so
session   required  pam_limits.so
session   required  pam_env.so
session   required  pam_unix.so
session   optional  pam_systemd.so
